Spec: SpecDD Highlighting Colors

Platform: IntelliJ Platform / Kotlin

Purpose:
  Define SpecDD highlighting attribute keys and theme-aware fallback attributes.

Owns:
  ./SpecDDHighlightingColors.kt

Can modify:
  ./SpecDDHighlightingColors.kt

Can read:
  /src/test/kotlin/ai/specdd/idea/highlighting/SpecDDHighlightingColorsBehaviorSpec.kt

Must:
  Define stable external names for every SpecDD highlighting key.
  Define a comment highlight key.
  Define an indentation highlight key.
  Define a continuation text highlight key.
  Define separate keys for default section labels, body key-value keys, meta section labels, positive section labels, negative section labels, required section labels, section colons, and section values.
  Define separate task marker keys for done, open, blocked, question, skipped, and invalid states.
  Define task id, scenario step, inline code span content, inline code span delimiter, path, symbol, and bad-character keys.
  Use non-deprecated `@TextAttributesKey` registration APIs.
  Assign each custom key a platform fallback key so normal editor schemes remain usable.
  Do not use bad-character fallbacks for valid blocked task or negative section tokens.
  Use platform bad-character fallback for invalid task markers and bad characters.
  Keep body key-value keys distinct from top-level section label keys.
  Cover external names, fallback keys, distinct keys, and invalid marker fallback in tests.

Must not:
  Tokenize text.
  Decide section label groups.
  Report validation diagnostics.
  Add plugin-specific settings.
